al_Square.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Old Spanish Fountain","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":36.141252,"lo":-5.354854,"d":501},{"n":"The Mario Finlayson Art Gallery","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":36.140892,"lo":-5.354562,"d":541},{"n":"Mario Finlayson National Art Gallery","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":36.140942,"lo":-5.354523,"d":542,"w":"https://www.culture.gi/art_galleries/mario-finlayson-national-art-gallery/"},{"n":"GEMA Art Gallery","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":36.144588,"lo":-5.354281,"d":543,"h":"Mo-Fr 09:00-15:00"},{"n":"Gibraltarian Women Monument","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":36.139052,"lo":-5.356144,"d":559},{"n":"Koehler Depression Carriage","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":36.14488,"lo":-5.353116,"d":652},{"n":"Gibraltar Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":36.138976,"lo":-5.354492,"d":667,"h":"Mo-Fr 10:00-18:00; Sa 10:00-14:00; Su off; PH off","w":"https://www.gibmuseum.gi","wp":"en:Gibraltar National Museum","ds":"The Gibraltar National Museum is a national museum of the history, culture and natural history of Gibraltar located within the city centre of the British overseas territory of Gibraltar. Founded in 1930 by the then Governor of Gibraltar, General Sir Alexander Godley, the museum houses an array of displays portraying The Rock's millennia-old history and the unique culture of its people.","wpu":"Gibraltar National Museum","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d4/Bomb_House.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Waterport Casemates","g":"sights","k":"fort","la":36.145791,"lo":-5.353354,"d":672},{"n":"Gibraltar Fine Arts Gallery","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":36.145252,"lo":-5.352776,"d":695,"ph":"+350 200 52126"},{"n":"Gustavo Bacarisas Exhibition Gallery","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":36.145334,"lo":-5.352705,"d":704,"w":"https://www.culture.gi/venues/gustavo-bacarisas-exhibition-gallery/"},{"n":"The Gibraltar Art Gallery","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":36.139478,"lo":-5.353346,"d":714,"h":"Mo-Su 11:00-15:00"},{"n":"Grand Casemates","g":"sights","k":"fort","la":36.145133,"lo":-5.352408,"d":721,"wp":"en:Grand Casemates","ds":"The Grand Casemates is a building in Grand Casemates Square, Gibraltar, that was originally a fortified barracks and casemate. It is beside Grand Casemates Gates, which leads through the former town wall.","wpu":"Grand Casemates","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Casemates_Square%2C_Gibraltar_%283%29.JPG/960px-Casemates_Square%2C_Gibraltar_%283%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"West Place of Arms","g":"sights","k":"fort","la":36.146258,"lo":-5.353042,"d":722,"ds":"The West Place of Arms is a place-of-arms in the British Overseas Territory of Gibraltar that was originally used as a troop assembly point. It is located in the gap between the North Bastion and its Counterguard, a structure built in 1804. The Counterguard provided defensive cover for the West Place of Arms, which was also fortified by a ditch into which a large caponier projected.","wpu":"West Place of Arms","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/West_Place_of_Arms.jpg/960px-West_Place_of_Arms.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Jones' Battery","g":"sights","k":"fort","la":36.143129,"lo":-5.351915,"d":726},{"n":"Wellington Front Right Bastion","g":"sights","k":"fort","la":36.137436,"lo":-5.354908,"d":769},{"n":"Queen Victoria Memorial","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":36.139322,"lo":-5.352702,"d":772},{"n":"Castle Batteries","g":"sights","k":"fort","la":36.144636,"lo":-5.351254,"d":806,"wp":"en:Castle Batteries","ds":"Castle Batteries are a series of artillery batteries that are part of the Northern Defences of the British Overseas Territory of Gibraltar. The batteries descend from the Moorish Castle to end at the sixth and seven batteries which are known as Crutchett's Batteries. There are brick vaulted bombproof rooms (casemates) under Crutchets Battery.","wpu":"Castle Batteries","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8a/6th_and_7th_Crutchett%27s_Batteries_Gibraltar.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Couvreport Battery","g":"sights","k":"fort","la":36.145057,"lo":-5.351097,"d":831,"wp":"en:Couvreport Battery","ds":"Couvreport Battery is an artillery battery in the British Overseas Territory of Gibraltar.","wpu":"Couvreport Battery","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Couvreporte_Battery.JPG/960px-Couvreporte_Battery.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Hanover Battery","g":"sights","k":"fort","la":36.144674,"lo":-5.350411,"d":880,"wp":"en:Hanover Battery","ds":"Hanover Battery was a casemated artillery battery on the north west part of the British Overseas Territory of Gibraltar. Beneath the battery was a tunnel known as Hanover Gallery.","wpu":"Hanover Battery","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/1870s_-_G._Washington_Wilson_-_Neutral_Ground.jpg/960px-1870s_-_G._Washington_Wilson_-_Neutral_Ground.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Moorish Castle","g":"sights","k":"castle","la":36.143861,"lo":-5.350151,"d":889,"wp":"en:Moorish Castle","ds":"The Moorish Castle is the name given to a medieval fortification in Gibraltar comprising various buildings, gates, and fortified walls, with the dominant features being the Tower of Homage and the Gate House. Part of the castle itself also housed the prison of Gibraltar until it was relocated in 2010.","wpu":"Moorish Castle","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/The_Moorish_Castle.jpg/960px-The_Moorish_Castle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Jones' Battery","g":"sights","k":"fort","la":36.143316,"lo":-5.349994,"d":899,"wp":"en:Jones' Battery","ds":"Jones' Battery is one of the best preserved of the \"retired\" artillery battery in the British Overseas Territory of Gibraltar. It was named after Sir John Thomas Jones who once controlled the fortifications here.","wpu":"Jones' Battery"},{"n":"Wellington Front Left Bastion","g":"sights","k":"fort","la":36.136227,"lo":-5.354441,"d":903},{"n":"Gibraltar","g":"sights","k":"zoo","la":36.142526,"lo":-5.34983,"d":914},{"n":"Queen Charlotte's Battery","g":"sights","k":"fort","la":36.144102,"lo":-5.349585,"d":943,"wp":"en:Queen Charlotte's Battery","ds":"Queen Charlotte's Battery is a 1727 artillery battery in the British Overseas Territory of Gibraltar.","wpu":"Queen Charlotte's Battery","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Queen_Charlottes_Battery.jpg/960px-Queen_Charlottes_Battery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"St Bernard's Hospital","g":"essentials","k":"hospital","la":36.143225,"lo":-5.35949,"d":52,"wp":"en:St Bernard's Hospital","ds":"St Bernard's Hospital is the only public hospital and teaching hospital in the British overseas territory of Gibraltar.","wpu":"St Bernard's Hospital","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/St_Bernard%27s_Hospital_with_GHA_Ambulances.jpg/960px-St_Bernard%27s_Hospital_with_GHA_Ambulances.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Morrisons Pharmacy","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":36.144396,"lo":-5.360212,"d":156,"w":"https://my.morrisons.com/storefinder/452/gibraltar"},{"n":"Morrisons","g":"essentials","k":"supermarket","la":36.144481,"lo":-5.360626,"d":174,"h":"Mo-Sa 07:00-23:00; Su 08:00-20:00","w":"https://my.morrisons.com/storefinder/452/gibraltar"},{"n":"Trafalgar Pharmacy (Europort)","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":36.142401,"lo":-5.358074,"d":185},{"n":"Valmar Pharmacy Europort","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":36.14341,