","la":36.140664,"lo":-5.352855,"d":692},{"n":"Duty Chemist","g":"essentials","k":"pharmacy","la":36.13913,"lo":-5.353729,"d":708},{"n":"Currency exchange","g":"essentials","k":"bureau_de_change","la":36.146658,"lo":-5.353214,"d":732},{"n":"Lloyds Bank","g":"essentials","k":"bank","la":36.147277,"lo":-5.352683,"d":811},{"n":"Mayfaironmain","g":"essentials","k":"hairdresser","la":36.137937,"lo":-5.35347,"d":812,"w":"http://www.mayfaironmain.gi","ph":"+35020075913","wifi":1},{"n":"Gibraltar North Mole Lighthouse","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":36.144154,"lo":-5.365775,"d":534,"ds":"The Gibraltar North Mole Lighthouse is one of several lighthouses in Gibraltar, the British Overseas Territory at the southern end of the Iberian Peninsula. Also referred to as the Gibraltar \"D\" Head Lighthouse, its cast-iron tower is painted black.","wpu":"Gibraltar North Mole Lighthouse","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0a/Gibraltar_North_Mole_Lighthouse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Algeciras Gate","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":36.139707,"lo":-5.354849,"d":589,"ds":"Algeciras Gate was a city gate in the British Overseas Territory of Gibraltar. It was located on the site of what later became King's Bastion and was removed during construction of the bastion by the Spanish in 1575. The Algeciras Gate was Moorish in style and adorned with detail, including motifs of keys.","wpu":"Algeciras Gate","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/King%27s_Bastion.jpg/960px-King%27s_Bastion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Coaling Island","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":36.1375,"lo":-5.3576,"d":648,"ds":"Coaling Island is an area of reclaimed land in the British Overseas Territory of Gibraltar. It is located at the centre of the western end of Gibraltar Harbour as one of its industrial zones. It also serves to harbour Cormorant Camber which berths small boats.","wpu":"Coaling Island","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Car_park_and_Quay_in_Gibraltar.JPG/960px-Car_park_and_Quay_in_Gibraltar.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Great Synagogue (Gibraltar)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":36.141828,"lo":-5.352511,"d":684,"ds":"The Great Synagogue of Gibraltar (Ladino: Esnoga Grande), also known as Kahal Kadosh Sha'ar HaShamayim (Hebrew: קהל קדוש שער השמיים, lit. 'Holy Congregation Gate of Heaven'; Ladino: Esnoga Sha'ar Hashamayim), is an Orthodox Jewish congregation and synagogue, located in the British overseas territory of Gibraltar.","wpu":"Great Synagogue (Gibraltar)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Great_Synagogue_2.jpg/960px-Great_Synagogue_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"North Mole, Gibraltar Harbour","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":36.1485,"lo":-5.3652,"d":769,"ds":"The North Mole is a breakwater located in the northern section of Gibraltar Harbour, in the British Overseas Territory of Gibraltar, at the southern end of the Iberian Peninsula. The North Mole, with the rest of harbour, is just north of the east entrance to the Strait of Gibraltar. The breakwater was formerly known as the Commercial Mole, and is the site of the commercial port in the harbour.","wpu":"North Mole, Gibraltar Harbour","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Bay_of_Gibraltar_from_The_Rock_8.JPG/960px-Bay_of_Gibraltar_from_The_Rock_8.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Gibraltar Detached Mole (\"B\" Head) Lighthouse","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":36.1357,"lo":-5.3641,"d":891,"ds":"The Gibraltar Detached Mole (\"B\" Head) Lighthouse is one of several lighthouses in Gibraltar, a British Overseas Territory at the south end of the Iberian Peninsula. The lighthouse is positioned west of the Rock of Gibraltar, on the Detached Mole at the south entrance to Gibraltar Harbour.","wpu":"Gibraltar Detached Mole (\"B\" Head) Lighthouse","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Part_of_the_port_in_gibraltar.JPG/960px-Part_of_the_port_in_gibraltar.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Gibraltar ( jih-BRAWL-tər, -⁠BROL-, Spanish: [xiβɾalˈtaɾ]) is a British Overseas Territory and city located near the southern tip of the Iberian Peninsula, on the Bay of Gibraltar, near the exit of the Mediterranean Sea into the Atlantic Ocean (Strait of Gibraltar). It has an area of 6.8 km2 (2.6 sq mi) and is bordered to the north by Spain (Campo de Gibraltar). The landscape is dominated by the Rock of Gibraltar, at the foot of which is a densely populated town area.","wpu":"Gibraltar","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Flag_of_Gibraltar.svg/960px-Flag_of_Gibraltar.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}